<title>USA: ABT Building in pact with steelworkers.</title>
<headline>ABT Building in pact with steelworkers.</headline>
<dateline>NEENAH, Wis. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABT Building Products Corp said Wednesday it has reached an agreement with the United Steelworkers of America, which represents the hourly manufacturing personnel at the company's Acton, Ontario, facility.</p>
<p>The new agreement is in effect through October 31, 2001.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available to provide In September 1996, ABT Building had reached an agreement through the year 2000 with the International Association of Machinists, which represents workers at its Alpena, Mich. plant.</p>
<p>ABT Building manufactures specialty building products including paneling and moulding made from engineered wood, plastics and fiber cement.</p>
</text>
